{
  "dom_id": "step-q77715",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/0b56d6a20b6a3e01dafa9770eb328ebaab5c14f76d87026c160c9be0d8926e74.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ is shown above. Which of the following is $\\overset{\u2015}{{A}^{\u2032}{B}^{\u2032}},$ the image of $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the image of $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{\u2032}(-3,7)$ and ${B}^{\u2032}(6,2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/ba458ff966132a67202469208f1daaaa98339ce22071247ca06d0f400c2e7390.png)",
